# Architecture

This document describes the project’s established components, boundaries,
dependency direction, data flow, ownership and material runtime constraints.
It must not describe hypothetical services, integrations or deployment
topology.

## Overview

[[ profile_values.ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW ]]

[[ profile_values.SYSTEM_DIAGRAM_SECTION ]]

The system diagram is generated only when it materially clarifies two or more
approved components or boundaries. Its accompanying text defines whether each
arrow represents dependency, runtime flow, data flow or authority. Different
arrow meanings must never be mixed silently.

## Components and ownership

[[ profile_values.COMPONENTS_AND_OWNERSHIP ]]

Each component owns one cohesive responsibility and exposes only the boundary
required by its consumers.

## Dependency direction

[[ profile_values.DEPENDENCY_DIRECTION ]]

Dependencies must remain directional. Cycles, hidden service location and
framework leakage across established boundaries are prohibited.

## Runtime and data flow

[[ profile_values.RUNTIME_DATA_FLOW ]]

Critical invariants must also be documented in text or tables. A diagram must
never be the only place an invariant is defined.

## Repository structure

[[ profile_values.DIRECTORY_TREE ]]

The directory tree describes repository layout; it is kept separate from the
system diagram, which describes runtime or dependency relationships.

## Runtime constraints

[[ profile_values.RUNTIME_CONSTRAINTS ]]

Document reliability, scale, latency, throughput, memory, concurrency,
atomicity and ordering constraints only when the approved project target makes
them material.

## Evolution rules

- Include only approved components, boundaries and external systems.
- Do not show speculative future integrations.
- Keep the diagram small and use standard Mermaid syntax without custom themes,
  icons or rendering plugins.
- Update this document in the same change as the architecture it represents.
- Add a sequence diagram only for a critical multi-step interaction.
- Add a state diagram only for a real lifecycle or state machine.
- Add a deployment diagram only after deployment topology is selected.
- Add a data-flow diagram only when sensitive data or trust boundaries require
  it.
